          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/fig5_analysis.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            22,
            51
          ]
        }
      ],
      "implementation_requirement": "Bind kinematic_field and24 ordered joint IDs. Keep angle and velocity metrics separate unless a prospectively specified aggregate explicitly defines them."
    },
    {
      "id": "pca_before_cv",
      "conclusion": "decode constructs all locked predictor trials, calls pca4Regression before cvRegress, and thus exposes held-out predictor samples to PCA. MATLAB pca centers inputs internally. pca4Regression parameter0.9 means floor(0.9*number_of_neurons), NOT90% explainedvariance; documented summary contradicts executable code. It subsequently applies random orthogonal rotation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/decode.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/decode.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            11,
            23
          ]
        },
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/pca4Regression.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/pca4Regression.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            6,
            16
          ]
        },
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/pca4Regression.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/pca4Regression.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            30,
            54
          ]
        }
      ],
      "implementation_requirement": "Fit centering, any scaling, PCA basis/dimensionality and any selected transform exclusively from designated training/calibration rows. A corrected pipeline must describe its PCA policy separately from author reproduction."
    },
    {
      "id": "neuron_selection",
      "conclusion": "loadDecode chooses100 neurons with smallest stored lift-event ZETA pvalues before calling decode. Source does not show fold-local recomputation of that selection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/loadDecode.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/loadDecode.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            12,
            25
          ]
        }
      ],
      "implementation_requirement": "Require fixed declaredcellbudget and training-only selection; do not reuse full-session published modulation scores as a leakage-safe selector."
    },
    {
      "id": "actual_fold_semantics",
      "conclusion": "decode passes nPartitions=10,nFolds=5; cvRegress uses modulus nPartitions and repermutates each10models. Actual operational pattern is five repetitions of tenfold trial splits (50fits), despite contradictory nFolds comments. Trials, not time rows, are split.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/decode.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/decode.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            20,
            23
          ]
        },
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/cvRegress.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/cvRegress.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            108,
            135
          ]
        }
      ],
      "implementation_requirement": "Bind explicit whole-trial train/test manifests and condition. Do not infer mathematicalfoldcount from misleading variable names."
    },
    {
      "id": "metric_distinction",
      "conclusion": "Author cvRegress uses1-var(y-yhat)/var(y), so constant predictionbias is removed from residual variance; this differs from1-SSE/SST R-squared. The benchmark specifies mouse-macro normalizedRMSE with secondary perjointR-squared but leaves normalization and pooling details unfrozen.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source_path": "main/fig5/analysis/cvRegress.m",
          "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kaufmanlab/GSK26-public/815b610b3beddfed5a3abf611d3a465ab9e4ce5c/main/fig5/analysis/cvRegress.m",
          "lines_1_based": [
            139,
            165
          ]
        }
      ],
      "implementation_requirement": "State metric equation, normalization reference/dof, zero-support policy, trial/time/session/joint weighting and mousemacro aggregation explicitly. Do not call the correctedmetric an exactauthor score."
    },
    {
      "id": "ridge_distinction",
      "conclusion": "Author ridgeMML selects a separate marginal-likelihoodlambda for each outcome after training-fold predictor standardization, with an unpenalizedintercept. A fixedalpha ridge or pooledlambda is a prospective reference family, not a port with establishedparity.",
